<h1>Round up</h1>
<h2>September 16, 2026</h2>
In today’s blog I touch on various topics.
<a name="2026-09-16-lindsay-clancy"> </a>
<h3>Lindsay Clancy</h3>
<p>Let’s look at some actual quotes from a couple of pro-Clancy women I
 found online. The first one comes from <a href="https://archive.ph/20260916132833/https://www.dailykos.com/stories/2026/9/5/800093197/community/this-week-in-the-war-on-women/">DailyKos</a>:
<blockquote>
<p>I have been reading several articles about Lindsay Clancy. The
 response from many men is very disturbing. It's like they can't even
 imagine hormones changing the way we think and feel.
</blockquote>
<p>The second one comes from <a href="https://archive.ph/20260826032640/https://www.reddit.com/r/TwoXChromosomes/comments/1vy4p22/my_bf_of_4_years_baited_me_into_forming_an/">Reddit</a>:
<blockquote>
<p>The fact that men are banding together to think that the answer is to
 deprive her of, yet again, the healthcare [Clancy] needs, is fucking
 terrifying.
</blockquote>
<p>In both cases, we see women who have an intense hatred of men, and
 want to blame men for Clancy murdering her own three kids with her own
 hands.
<p>As you can imagine, <a href="AI-summaries/2026-09-16-Clancy.html">the radical right is having a field day with the whole Lindsay Clancy  issue</a>, 
falsely claiming supporting Clancy is some kind of mainstream
 feminist cause.
<p>Yes, there <em>are</em> women out there with an intense and
 unreasonable hatred of men. I have had the dubious pleasure of knowing
 many of those kinds of women; needless to say, they are no longer in my
 life. However, the majority of women aren’t like that, and the women in
 my circle of friends simply have no issue on Lindsay Clancy. The one
 female friend I have with an opinion on Clancy feels her actions were
 immoral and vile.
<a name="2026-09-16-twitter-and-reddit-scrapers"> </a>
<h3>Twitter and Reddit scrapers</h3>
<p>Now that both Reddit and Twitter need people to log in to read
 content on their sites, and now that Twitter is playing the
 whack-a-mole game trying to take down Twitter scrapers, I will provide
 both <a href="https://codeberg.org/mv12star/shitter/wiki/Instances">a list of Twitter scrapers</a> 
and a list of <a href="https://github.com/redlib-org/redlib-instances/blob/main/instances.md">Reddit  scrapers</a>.
<a name="2026-09-16-viva-mxico"> </a>
<h3>¡Viva México!</h3>
<p>Last night I celebrated Mexico’s independence with my family. We had
 a lovely evening. Amazing how much more stable, balanced, and loving
 people are in real life compared the the monsters we have online.


